--- body ---
## Context
Ticket 1121 moved live ticket counts out of STATE.md and into
`scripts/on-start.sh`, which prints them at session start. Only Claude Code
runs that script today (SessionStart hook via the adapter plugin). Codex and
Pi sessions therefore see no ticket counts, and none of the other startup
context the script assembles (disk headroom, loader reminder).

1121 made the script runtime-neutral where it was safe: the ticket counts use
the working directory when `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` is unset, and the
Claude-specific lines (worktree instruction citing rules/claude-code.md,
effort read from ~/.claude/settings.json) print only when
`CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` is set.

## Scope
1. First confirm, per runtime, that Codex and Pi expose a session-start event
   whose output reaches the model as context (documented event, measured on
   the installed version). If a runtime has none, record that and stop for
   that runtime; the wrapper's pre-launch probe is not a substitute, since its
   stdout goes to the terminal, not the conversation.
2. Wire the event to `scripts/on-start.sh` in `adapters/codex/` and/or
   `adapters/pi/`.
3. Revisit the blocks still keyed on `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` alone (coherence
   prompt, memory-index injection, local-main sync report, the post-cutoff
   git hooks and sync): decide whether each should fall back to the working
   directory or the runtime's own project variable.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Session-start event confirmed or ruled out for Codex and for Pi, with evidence
- [ ] Where one exists, a session in that runtime shows the live ticket-counts line
- [ ] rules/state.md no longer says Codex and Pi do not wire a hook (or names the runtime that cannot)
